course: dictionary
lesson: 8430
title: Sacs: small bags inside living things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A sac is a small bag-like part inside a plant or animal. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it. «A wolf spider mother carries her egg sac, and when the babies hatch they ride on her back» tells you a sac holds something, because the babies come out of it.
explain: Read «Inside the lungs ... end in hundreds of millions of tiny air sacs, where oxygen slips into the blood». The clue is air: a sac can be filled with air, and oxygen passes through its thin walls. Sacs are often filled with liquid or air, like a little bag holding something inside.
explain: In science, sac is the special word for this bag. In everyday talk people say bag or pouch. So when you see sac, think "a small bag inside a living thing", then swap in bag and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A sac is a small bag-like part inside a plant or animal.
fact: Sacs are often filled with liquid or air.
fact: «Egg sac» means a silk bag that a spider uses to hold its eggs.
fact: «Ink sac» means the part of a squid or octopus that stores dark ink, which it squirts to escape enemies.
fact: Your lungs have hundreds of millions of tiny air sacs, where oxygen passes into your blood.
exercise: «A wolf spider mother carries her egg sac, and when the babies hatch they ride on her back.» What is an egg sac? | A spider's leg | A web for catching flies | A hard shell the babies bite open | *A silk bag that holds the eggs
exercise: «In a squid or octopus, the ink sac squirts dark ink to escape enemies.» Why does an octopus squirt ink? | To keep its eggs warm | *To escape enemies | To help it sleep | To make its colour bright for a party
exercise: «Octopuses have tiny colour sacs in their skin that muscles stretch open or squeeze shut.» Which everyday word could you swap in for sac here? | Leaf | Feather | *Bag | Bone
test: «Spiders make silk ... such as sticky threads, strong frame threads and egg sacs.» Which job do egg sacs do? | Hold the spider's legs | *Hold a spider's eggs | Make the silk stickier | Catch flies in the wind
test: «Some octopuses can match their background in less than a second.» What helps them do this? | Their hard shell | Their ink, squirted over the rocks | Air sacs in their lungs | *Colour sacs in their skin that muscles stretch open or squeeze shut
exam: «A honeybee's venom sac keeps pumping while its sting stays in the skin, so the sting must be scraped out quickly.» Why must the sting be scraped out as soon as possible? | Because the skin will heal faster with a sting in it | Because stings are useful for keeping | *Because the venom sac keeps pumping while it stays in | Because the bee needs the sting to fly
